comments.body:
🌿 method packet for Cael execution — `R-CW-DELEGATE-TOKEN` / bca2b0b

Purpose: prove the bracket/token sibling of `R-CW-DELEGATE-SELF-CONTINUATION`. A `continue_delegate` child must schedule its own continuation by emitting a `CONTINUE_WORK:N` / `[[CONTINUE_WORK:N]]` token in reply text, then actually receive the follow-up child turn and return a sentinel. This row is not satisfied by typed `continue_work()`.

Recommended fire shape:

1. From the Cael parent Discord session, call typed `continue_delegate(mode="silent-wake", fanoutMode="tree")` with a child task like:

   ```text
   R-CW-DELEGATE-TOKEN proof fire for docs#221 / candidate bca2b0b89ab886bf23a10e4983926f6b374b3188.
   Sentinel: R-CW-DELEGATE-TOKEN-BCA2B0B-CAEL-<timestamp>.
   Do not call typed continue_work. In your first child reply, emit exactly one continuation token at the end of the text: CONTINUE_WORK:5 (or [[CONTINUE_WORK:5]] if that is the parser form you are testing). After the continuation wake arrives, return the sentinel plus session key, hop/flow metadata, and any visible token/trace metadata. Do not spawn further children.
   ```

2. PASS byte requires all of:
   - parent `continue_delegate` scheduled and spawned a child session;
   - child first turn transcript contains the bracket/token election text, with no typed `continue_work` tool call used for the row;
   - gateway/journal/parser evidence shows the child token was parsed as continuation work (`origin=token` / `kind=work` or equivalent current-byte wording);
   - durable `flow_runs` row for `core/continuation-work` is owned by the child session, reaches `status=succeeded`, `current_step="Same-session continuation turn granted"`, `disposition=granted`, realistic low hop (`1/200` expected), and `busySkipCount=0` unless a captured anomaly explains otherwise;
   - child receives an actual second continuation turn and returns `R-CW-DELEGATE-TOKEN-BCA2B0B-CAEL-<timestamp>`;
   - parent targeted-return / fanout receipt reaches the parent chain;
   - Tempo includes parent delegate trace plus child continuation work/fire trace. A `continue_work` tool span is not expected for the token path; if present, explain why it does not invalidate the token proof.

3. Evidence package requirements:
   - `EVIDENCE.md` with honest scope and verdict;
   - parent delegate receipt JSON;
   - child/subagent transcript excerpt showing first-turn token emission and second-turn sentinel return;
   - subagent list/history receipts;
   - `flow-runs-matching.tsv` + full JSONL for delegate, mirrored child, and continuation-work rows;
   - journal excerpt around delegate spawn, token parse/effective signal, work hedge/wake, token accumulation, and targeted return;
   - Tempo trace JSON + span summaries;
   - exact `source/source-sha.txt`, `source/source-commit.txt`, and `version.txt` for `OpenClaw 2026.6.11 (bca2b0b)`;
   - if any TaskFlow/gateway anomaly appears, file a fresh `karmaterminal/openclaw` issue with byte evidence and link it from the proof.

Do not package PASS if the token is merely stripped/recognized but no real child continuation turn executes. That is a bug/anomaly capture, not a PASS. If a packaging step would itself schedule more continuation work inside the proof child, stop and package from the parent/outside instead so the terminal byte stays clean.
